& [IR8ManagerOrchestrationBoundaryImportAndProofReconciliationV1] is the IR8-S01 boundary map for integrated manager orchestration planning
  + [boundary_map_id] is ir8-manager-orchestration-boundary-import-and-proof-reconciliation-v1
  + [boundary_map_uuid] is 087a7a64-b292-471e-b8a6-471e4b4a3d1e
  + [slice_id] is IR8-S01
  + [source_chunk] is IR8 integrated manager orchestration planning
  + [authority_scope] is imported parser/projection proof, imported operator harness proof, imported LangGraph proof runtime boundary, imported surface projection proof, imported coordination mailbox proof, imported operations dry-run proof, post-IR7 readiness gates, manager authority ladder, proof-pack interaction rules, stale triggers, and forbidden mutation boundaries
  + [implementation_scope] is boundary import and invariant reconciliation only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: import accepted IR2 through IR7 proof boundaries before defining manager loop, readiness, packet, coordination handoff, surface handoff, operations dry-run handoff, fixture, implementation, or activation contracts
  = must: preserve source authority, derived projections, graph execution checkpoints, coordination carriers, dry-run outputs, and generated reports as separate record classes
  = must: preserve manager-loop outputs as planning and proof records, not commands, dispatch authority, completion authority, operations authority, or live-control authority
  = must: preserve coordination claims as work-boundary records that constrain readiness and conflict review but cannot dispatch agents or jobs
  = must: preserve dry-run-only operations semantics and live-control refusal when manager plans resemble dispatch, process control, job control, GPU control, model runtime control, or machine-control authority
  - never: implement manager orchestration code, execute manager loops, create fixture files, create expected ledgers, create generated outputs, install dependencies, mutate package metadata, implement adapters, implement transports, implement UI, dispatch agents, dispatch jobs, execute commands, control processes, control GPU, mutate model runtimes, access credentials, mutate network exposure, perform destructive filesystem actions, create persistent operations automation, authorize operations control, or authorize live machine control in this slice

