& [ReconciledIR8InvariantSet] is the reconciled invariant set for integrated manager orchestration planning
  + [invariant] is SOP source documents, accepted canonical specifications, accepted packs, accepted proofs, accepted completion reviews, accepted human override records, and SJS-signed artifacts remain source authority
  + [invariant] is parser and projection outputs describe source-derived structure but cannot create authority without accepted source, canonical signature, or completion review
  + [invariant] is operator traces are execution evidence only and require accepted operator contracts and proof review before they can affect readiness
  + [invariant] is LangGraph checkpoint state stores procedure state and kernel references, not source truth, dispatch authority, or live-control authority
  + [invariant] is manager loop records may recompute readiness, propose work packets, request SOP-first interrupts, and emit proof obligations, but they cannot execute work or accept completion by themselves
  + [invariant] is work packets are bounded candidate assignments until accepted by source authority, readiness proof, coordination claim rules, and completion review gates
  + [invariant] is surface projections display authority notice, freshness state, blockers, faults, claims, and proof state but cannot mutate canonical authority directly
  + [invariant] is coordination claims coordinate work boundaries only and cannot dispatch agents, run commands, mutate resources, or accept completion
  + [invariant] is operation requests and dry-run results remain operations planning records and cannot approve live effects
  + [invariant] is human approval records must remain explicit, fresh, scoped, revocable, and tied to rollback or abort routes before they can be considered as future safety inputs
  + [invariant] is broad approval, stale approval, fixture success, dry-run success, graph checkpoint state, projected user intent, mailbox notice, active claim, or carrier state cannot authorize dispatch or live control
  + [invariant] is manager orchestration must route ambiguous authority, stale proof, hidden scope expansion, contested claims, dry-run/live-control confusion, and generated-output promotion through SOP-first interrupt, coordination review, completion review, or rebake
  + [invariant] is live-control escalation requires separate future source preservation, SJS processing, least-privilege credential boundary, rollback proof, explicit human approval rules, monitoring and abort routes, and completion review

  = must: preserve these invariants through IR8-S02 through IR8-S06
  = must: route invariant contradictions through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

& [ManagerAuthorityLadder: IR8] is the authority ladder that all downstream IR8 contracts must preserve
  + [authority_tier] is source_authority
  + [source_authority_member] is preserved source specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted canonical specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted SJS satisfaction signature
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted proof pack
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted completion review
  + [source_authority_member] is explicit accepted human override record with authority notice
  + [authority_tier] is manager_planning_record
  + [manager_planning_record_member] is readiness_projection
  + [manager_planning_record_member] is work_packet_candidate
  + [manager_planning_record_member] is proof_obligation
  + [manager_planning_record_member] is SOP_first_interrupt_context
  + [manager_planning_record_member] is completion_review_gate
  + [authority_tier] is accepted_execution_evidence
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is operator_trace accepted through proof or completion review
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is fixture_result accepted through proof or completion review
  + [authority_tier] is coordination_boundary_record
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is coordination_claim
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is mailbox_carrier_context
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is conflict_review_context
  + [authority_tier] is operations_planning_record
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is operation_request
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is dry_run_result
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is refusal_record
  + [operations_planning_record_member] is resource_safety_review
  + [authority_tier] is generated_projection_evidence
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated surface projection
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated dry-run projection
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated manager report
  + [authority_tier] is graph_checkpoint_context
  + [graph_checkpoint_context_member] is procedure_state
  + [graph_checkpoint_context_member] is node_resume_pointer
  + [graph_checkpoint_context_member] is kernel_record_reference
  + [authority_tier] is carrier_context
  + [carrier_context_member] is terminal output
  + [carrier_context_member] is chat message
  + [carrier_context_member] is Codex thread state
  + [carrier_context_member] is mailbox path
  + [carrier_context_member] is UI event
  + [carrier_context_member] is IRC log
  + [carrier_context_member] is Matrix event

  = must: display lower authority tier and trust limit anywhere lower-tier records may influence action
  = must: prevent lower tiers from satisfying source-authority, dispatch, completion, operations-control, or live-control obligations without separate accepted authority

& [ProofPackInteractionMap: IR8] is the imported proof-pack handoff map for downstream manager contracts
  + [proof_pack] is IR2 parser and projection implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is source parsing and projection identity evidence for manager input normalization
  + [manager_limit] is parsed projection is not source authority unless backed by accepted source and canonical signature
  + [proof_pack] is IR3 operator harness implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is deterministic operator execution and trace evidence pattern
  + [manager_limit] is operator trace is evidence, not completion acceptance without review
  + [proof_pack] is IR4 LangGraph proof runtime implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is graph node flow, checkpoint, interrupt, and proof-of-shape pattern
  + [manager_limit] is checkpoint state is procedure context, not authority
  + [proof_pack] is IR5 surface projection implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, and conversation projection pattern
  + [manager_limit] is surface state is projection evidence, not mutation authority
  + [proof_pack] is IR6 coordination mailbox implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is claim, mailbox, rendezvous, conflict, stale, and human override projection pattern
  + [manager_limit] is carrier state and claim state constrain coordination only and do not dispatch work
  + [proof_pack] is IR7 operations dry-run simulator implementation proof
  + [manager_use] is operation request, resource safety, refusal, generated path, fixture runner, and no-live-effect proof
  + [manager_limit] is dry-run success is not live approval or dispatch authority

  = must: require IR8-S02 to define the manager loop contract before any fixture plan, implementation plan, or activation pack can consume this interaction map
  = must: reject any proof-pack merge that collapses record classes or authority tiers

& [IR8GeneratedOutputAndFixtureBoundary] is the generated-output and fixture boundary for IR8-S01
  + [fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [future_fixture_slice] is IR8-S04 after IR8-S01 through IR8-S03 acceptance
  + [future_generated_output_policy_slice] is IR8-S05 after IR8-S04 acceptance
  + [current_generated_output_role] is none_created_by_this_slice
  + [future_generated_output_default_authority] is non_authoritative_projection_only

  = must: reject IR8-S01 completion if fixture sources, expected ledgers, generated output files, manager reports, carrier caches, or projection reports are created
  = must: require later accepted generated-output policy before any generated manager projection root can be trusted even as disposable evidence

& [ForbiddenIR8S01MutationList] is the forbidden mutation set for IR8-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted IR2, IR3, IR4, IR5, IR6, IR7, FSC5, post-IR7, or IR8 authority inputs to make reconciliation easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating parsed projections as source authority without accepted source and canonical signature
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating operator traces as completion acceptance without review
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating graph checkpoints as authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating surface projections as mutation authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating coordination claims, mailbox carriers, or conflict reviews as dispatch authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating operation requests or dry-run results as commands or live approval
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing manager orchestration code
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating fixture source files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating expected ledger files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating generated output files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing dependencies or mutating package metadata
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing adapters, transports, UI, or live surfaces
  + [forbidden_mutation] is executing commands
  + [forbidden_mutation] is starting, stopping, killing, or reprioritizing live processes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is launching, cancelling, or scheduling GPU workloads
  + [forbidden_mutation] is starting, stopping, installing, upgrading, or configuring model runtimes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching agents or jobs
  + [forbidden_mutation] is accessing, writing, rotating, or mutating credentials or secrets
  + [forbidden_mutation] is opening, exposing, or mutating network listeners or firewall state
  + [forbidden_mutation] is performing destructive filesystem actions
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating persistent operations automation
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control

  = must: fail IR8-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR8] is the stale trigger set for downstream IR8 work
  + [stale_trigger] is IR8 canonical specification hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR8 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR8 minting review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is post-IR7 readiness surface or review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR2 through IR7 implementation proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR7 implementation completion review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC5 operations safety pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is parser projection treated as source authority without canonical backing
  + [stale_trigger] is operator trace treated as completion acceptance
  + [stale_trigger] is graph checkpoint treated as source authority
  + [stale_trigger] is surface projection treated as mutation authority
  + [stale_trigger] is coordination claim or mailbox carrier treated as dispatch authority
  + [stale_trigger] is dry-run result treated as live approval
  + [stale_trigger] is manager output treated as command execution, job dispatch, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, credential mutation, network mutation, destructive filesystem action, operations control, or live-control effect

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

